# Copy to `.env` and fill in. Never commit the filled-in file — .gitignore
# covers `.env*` and makes an exception only for this template.
#
# astro.config.mjs bridges these into process.env at startup (Astro loads .env
# into import.meta.env only, which this project deliberately does not read for
# secrets). A real environment variable always wins over anything set here, so
# this file has no effect on Vercel.

# Fine-grained personal access token, PUBLIC REPOSITORIES (READ-ONLY), no
# account permissions — the GitHub panel on `/` reads nothing private.
#
# Optional. Without it the panel still works, on GitHub's unauthenticated
# limit of 60 requests/hour counted PER IP — which in local development is
# shared with `gh` and anything else on your connection, and is easy to
# exhaust while iterating. With it, 5,000/hour against the token.
GITHUB_TOKEN=
